.TH "CLOSEWATCHER.CLOSE" "3JS" "March 2, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CloseWatcher.close \- CloseWatcher: close() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]close()\f[B]\f[R] method of the \f[CR]CloseWatcher\f[R]
interface lets you skip any logic in the \f[CR]cancel\f[R] event handler
and immediately fire the \f[CR]close\f[R] event.
It then deactivates the close watcher as if \f[CR]destroy()\f[R] was
called.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
close()
.EE
.SS Parameters
None.
.SS Return value
None (\f[CR]undefined\f[R]).
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Using the \f[CR]close()\f[R] method
Use the \f[CR]close()\f[R] method to deactivate the close watcher and
destroy it.
.IP
.EX
watcher.close();
.EE
